, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/11/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/7dd20b952257a3355c728716113cff772f7c5185/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Problem: `to_cents` truncates float error (`19.99 * 100 == 1998.9999\u2026` \u2192 `1998`). Fix: round to nearest cent.\npytest isn't installed, so I run the test functions directly:\nI fixed the bug, which was in `ledger/currency.py`. `to_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, which cuts off the decimals instead of rounding. Floats can't store prices like these exactly, so the product comes out just under the right value and the cut drops a cent:\n\n- `19.99 * 100` gives `1998.999\u2026`, which became `1998`\n- `0.29 * 100` gives `28.999\u2026`, which became `28`, so 3 of them came to `84` instead of `87`\n- `4.35 * 100` gives `434.999\u2026`, which became `434`\n\nThe fix is `round(amount * 100)`. Every price goes through this function, so line, discount and tax totals now start from the correct cents.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions in `tests/test_totals.py` and `tests/test_report.py` directly. All 5 passed.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 70196, "requests_cache_write": 5671, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0653102, "requests_c